meta {
  name: Delete Custom Technique
  type: http
  seq: 17
}

delete {
  url: {{baseURL}}/v1/house/:house/incidents/custom-technique/:techniqueId
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:path {
  house: 4
  techniqueId: 1
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

docs {
  # Delete Custom Method/Technique

  Soft-deletes a custom intervention technique. Only custom techniques can be deleted (not default ones).
  Requires appropriate permissions (update_incident).

  ## Path Parameters:
  - `house` - House ID
  - `youngPersonId` - Young person ID
  - `techniqueId` - The ID of the custom technique to delete

  ## Authorization:
  Must have `update_incident` permission.

  ## Response Success:
  ```json
  {
    "success": true,
    "message": "Custom technique deleted successfully",
    "data": null
  }
  ```

  ## Response Error (Not Found):
  ```json
  {
    "success": false,
    "message": "Technique not found or unauthorized",
    "data": null
  }
  ```

  ## Notes:
  - Only affects custom techniques (built-in options cannot be deleted)
  - Uses soft delete, so technique can be restored by re-adding it with same name
  - Deleted techniques will not appear in GET /method-technique-options
  - User must have access to the house or client that owns the technique
}
